IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `au-interpretation-time`

-- Tests for au-interpretation-time.l4. EVERY expected value is written by hand from
-- the text (the section and example are named beside it), and weekdays were taken
-- from a calendar, not from the encoding. A failing assertion is a finding.

`no closures` MEANS `Days of closure` OF EMPTY, EMPTY

§ `Section 2B: business day, calendar month, calendar year, financial year`

-- 2026-02-02 is a Monday, 2026-01-31 a Saturday, 2026-02-01 a Sunday.
#ASSERT `is a business day` (Date 2 2 2026) EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT (`is a business day` (Date 31 1 2026) EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a business day` (Date 1 2 2026) EMPTY)
-- A Monday that is a public holiday in the place is not a business day.
#ASSERT NOT (`is a business day` (Date 1 6 2026) (LIST Date 1 6 2026))
#ASSERT `is a business day` (Date 2 6 2026) (LIST Date 1 6 2026)
-- "calendar month means one of the 12 months of the year".
#ASSERT `is one of the 12 calendar months` 1
#ASSERT `is one of the 12 calendar months` 12
#ASSERT NOT (`is one of the 12 calendar months` 0)
#ASSERT NOT (`is one of the 12 calendar months` 13)
#ASSERT NOT (`is one of the 12 calendar months` 1.5)
-- "calendar year means a period of 12 months starting on 1 January".
#ASSERT `the calendar year containing` (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS `A span of days` OF (Date 1 1 2026), (Date 31 12 2026)
-- "financial year means a period of 12 months starting on 1 July".
#ASSERT `the financial year containing` (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS `A span of days` OF (Date 1 7 2025), (Date 30 6 2026)
#ASSERT `the financial year containing` (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS `A span of days` OF (Date 1 7 2026), (Date 30 6 2027)
#ASSERT `the financial year containing` (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS `A span of days` OF (Date 1 7 2025), (Date 30 6 2026)

§ `Section 2G: months (the four printed examples, then the edges)`

-- 2G(1) example 1: a month starting on 15 December ends immediately before 15 January.
#ASSERT `the last day of a month starting on` (Date 15 12 2025) EQUALS Date 14 1 2026
-- 2G(1) example 2: a month starting on 31 August ends at the end of September.
#ASSERT `the last day of a month starting on` (Date 31 8 2025) EQUALS Date 30 9 2025
-- 2G(2) example 1: 6 months starting on 15 December end immediately before 15 June.
#ASSERT `the last day of` 6 `calendar months starting on` (Date 15 12 2025) EQUALS Date 14 6 2026
-- 2G(2) example 2: 6 months starting on 31 October end at the end of April.
#ASSERT `the last day of` 6 `calendar months starting on` (Date 31 10 2025) EQUALS Date 30 4 2026
-- A month starting on the 1st ends on the last day of the same month.
#ASSERT `the last day of a month starting on` (Date 1 3 2025) EQUALS Date 31 3 2025
-- 29, 30 and 31 January: no corresponding day in a short February.
#ASSERT `the last day of a month starting on` (Date 29 1 2025) EQUALS Date 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `the last day of a month starting on` (Date 30 1 2025) EQUALS Date 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `the last day of a month starting on` (Date 31 1 2025) EQUALS Date 28 2 2025
-- In a leap year 29 February exists: a month starting on 29 January ends immediately before it.
#ASSERT `the last day of a month starting on` (Date 29 1 2024) EQUALS Date 28 2 2024
#ASSERT `the last day of a month starting on` (Date 30 1 2024) EQUALS Date 29 2 2024
#ASSERT `the last day of a month starting on` (Date 31 1 2024) EQUALS Date 29 2 2024
-- Across the end of a year.
#ASSERT `the last day of` 12 `calendar months starting on` (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS Date 31 12 2025
#ASSERT `the last day of` 13 `calendar months starting on` (Date 15 12 2025) EQUALS Date 14 1 2027
#ASSERT `the last day of` 2 `calendar months starting on` (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS Date 28 2 2026
-- Starting on a leap day: 12 months end at the end of February 2025; 48 months end
-- immediately before 29 February 2028.
#ASSERT `the last day of` 12 `calendar months starting on` (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS Date 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `the last day of` 48 `calendar months starting on` (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS Date 28 2 2028

§ `Section 36(1): the table of seven items`

-- Items 1 to 4 include the specified day; items 5 to 7 do not.
#ASSERT `a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` `between two days`
#ASSERT `a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` `begins at, on or with a specified day`
#ASSERT `a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` `continues until a specified day`
#ASSERT `a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` `ends at, on or with a specified day`
#ASSERT NOT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` `begins from a specified day`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` `begins after a specified day`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` `ends before a specified day`)
-- Example 1: between 1 September and 30 November, both days count.
#ASSERT `the first day of the period` `between two days` (Date 1 9 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 9 2026)
#ASSERT `the last day of the period` `between two days` (Date 30 11 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 30 11 2026)
-- Example 2: a permission that begins on the first day of a financial year is in force on that day.
#ASSERT `the first day of the period` `begins at, on or with a specified day` (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 7 2026)
-- Example 3: a licence that continues until 31 March is valid up to and including 31 March.
#ASSERT `the last day of the period` `continues until a specified day` (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 3 2026)
-- Example 4: a right that ends on the last day of a financial year may be exercised on that day.
#ASSERT `the last day of the period` `ends at, on or with a specified day` (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 30 6 2026)
-- Example 5: expressed to operate from 30 June, it starts to operate on 1 July.
#ASSERT `the first day of the period` `begins from a specified day` (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 7 2026)
-- Example 6: a decision made on 2 August and 28 days after the day it is made: the period begins on 3 August.
#ASSERT `the first day of the period` `begins after a specified day` (Date 2 8 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 3 8 2026)
-- Example 7: the 7 days before the day a proceeding starts on 8 May run from 1 May to 7 May.
#ASSERT `the last day of the period` `ends before a specified day` (Date 8 5 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 7 5 2026)
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 7 Days `starting on` (Date 1 5 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 7 5 2026)
-- A start expression gives no last day, and an end expression gives no first day.
#ASSERT `the last day of the period` `begins from a specified day` (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the first day of the period` `ends before a specified day` (Date 8 5 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Lengths: days, months, and what the text does not say (weeks, years)`

-- A period of 1 day starting on a day is that day; 28 days starting 3 August end on 30 August (examples 6 and 7).
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 Days `starting on` (Date 3 8 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 3 8 2026)
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 28 Days `starting on` (Date 3 8 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 30 8 2026)
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 3 Months `starting on` (Date 15 12 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 14 3 2026)
-- Weeks and years: the Act does not give their length (it never uses the word week).
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 2 Weeks `starting on` (Date 3 8 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 3 Years `starting on` (Date 17 7 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A length that is not a whole number of at least 1 has no last day.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 0 Days `starting on` (Date 3 8 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` (0 MINUS 5) Months `starting on` (Date 3 8 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1.5 Days `starting on` (Date 3 8 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `The worked cases (NOTES.md answer table)`

-- W1 three years from 2025-07-16: the first day is 2025-07-17 (item 5); the Act gives no length for a year.
#ASSERT `the first day of the period` `begins from a specified day` (Date 16 7 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 17 7 2025)
#ASSERT `the last day of a counted period of` 3 Years `that` `begins from a specified day` (Date 16 7 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- ... on the ALTERNATIVE reading (a year is 12 months): 36 months from 2025-07-17 end immediately before 2028-07-17.
#ASSERT `ALTERNATIVE READING: the last day of a counted period, expressed as` `begins from a specified day` (Date 16 7 2025) 3 Years EQUALS JUST (Date 16 7 2028)
-- W2 five years from 2025-01-15 and from 2025-09-01 (alternative reading).
#ASSERT `ALTERNATIVE READING: the last day of a counted period, expressed as` `begins from a specified day` (Date 15 1 2025) 5 Years EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2030)
#ASSERT `ALTERNATIVE READING: the last day of a counted period, expressed as` `begins from a specified day` (Date 1 9 2025) 5 Years EQUALS JUST (Date 1 9 2030)
#ASSERT `the last day of a counted period of` 5 Years `that` `begins from a specified day` (Date 15 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- W3 thirty days from 2026-01-01: the first day is 2026-01-02 and the last day 2026-01-31, a Saturday.
#ASSERT `the last day of a counted period of` 30 Days `that` `begins from a specified day` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)
-- ... which s 36(2) moves to Monday 2026-02-02 (Sunday 1 February is also a rest day).
#ASSERT `the last day on which the thing may be done` TRUE (Date 31 1 2026) `no closures` EQUALS Date 2 2 2026
-- ... and to Tuesday 3 February if Monday 2 February is a public holiday.
#ASSERT `the last day on which the thing may be done` TRUE (Date 31 1 2026) (`Days of closure` OF (LIST Date 2 2 2026), EMPTY) EQUALS Date 3 2 2026
-- W4 two years from 2024-02-28: the first day is 2024-02-29; alternative reading: 24 months, no 29 February in 2026.
#ASSERT `the first day of the period` `begins from a specified day` (Date 28 2 2024) EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2024)
#ASSERT `ALTERNATIVE READING: the last day of a counted period, expressed as` `begins from a specified day` (Date 28 2 2024) 2 Years EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2026)
#ASSERT `the last day of a counted period of` 2 Years `that` `begins from a specified day` (Date 28 2 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
-- ... 2026-02-28 is a Saturday: s 36(2) moves it to Monday 2026-03-02.
#ASSERT `the last day on which the thing may be done` TRUE (Date 28 2 2026) `no closures` EQUALS Date 2 3 2026
-- W5 one year from 2024-02-29: the first day is 2024-03-01; alternative reading: 12 months end immediately before 1 March 2025.
#ASSERT `ALTERNATIVE READING: the last day of a counted period, expressed as` `begins from a specified day` (Date 29 2 2024) 1 Years EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2025)
-- W6 one month from 2025-01-31: the first day is 2025-02-01; the month ends immediately before 1 March: 2025-02-28.
#ASSERT `the first day of the period` `begins from a specified day` (Date 31 1 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 2 2025)
#ASSERT `the last day of a counted period of` 1 Months `that` `begins from a specified day` (Date 31 1 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2025)
-- 2025-02-28 is a Friday: no s 36(2) move.
#ASSERT `the last day on which the thing may be done` TRUE (Date 28 2 2025) `no closures` EQUALS Date 28 2 2025

§ `Fork F1: does "one month from 15 December" count 15 December? (item 5 says it does not)`

-- 2G alone ("a month starting on 15 December") ends on 14 January; item 5 composed with 2G
-- ("one month from 15 December") begins on 16 December and ends on 15 January.
#ASSERT `the last day of a month starting on` (Date 15 12 2025) EQUALS Date 14 1 2026
#ASSERT `the last day of a counted period of` 1 Months `that` `begins from a specified day` (Date 15 12 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2026)
#ASSERT `the last day of a counted period of` 1 Months `that` `begins at, on or with a specified day` (Date 15 12 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 14 1 2026)
#ASSERT `the last day of a counted period of` 1 Months `that` `begins after a specified day` (Date 15 12 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2026)

§ `Fork F3: s 36(2) reaches a last day counted in months or years as well as in days`

-- One month from 2026-01-31 ends on Saturday 2026-02-28; the thing may be done on Monday 2026-03-02.
#ASSERT `the last day of a counted period of` 1 Months `that` `begins from a specified day` (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2026)
#ASSERT `the last day on which the thing may be done` TRUE (Date 28 2 2026) `no closures` EQUALS Date 2 3 2026

§ `Section 36(2) and (3)`

-- The text's own example: 31 March is a Saturday (2018), so the thing may be done on Monday 2 April.
#ASSERT `the last day on which the thing may be done` TRUE (Date 31 3 2018) `no closures` EQUALS Date 2 4 2018
-- A weekday last day does not move.
#ASSERT `the last day on which the thing may be done` TRUE (Date 2 2 2026) `no closures` EQUALS Date 2 2 2026
-- Limb (a) not met (no Act requires or allows the thing): the rule does not move the day.
#ASSERT `the last day on which the thing may be done` FALSE (Date 31 3 2018) `no closures` EQUALS Date 31 3 2018
-- Several days in a row: Friday 2026-04-03 and Monday 2026-04-06 are holidays; Saturday and Sunday between: the next day is Tuesday 7 April.
#ASSERT `the last day on which the thing may be done` TRUE (Date 3 4 2026) (`Days of closure` OF (LIST Date 3 4 2026, Date 6 4 2026), EMPTY) EQUALS Date 7 4 2026
-- If the office is also closed for the whole of Tuesday 7 April, the next day is Wednesday 8 April.
#ASSERT `the last day on which the thing may be done` TRUE (Date 3 4 2026) (`Days of closure` OF (LIST Date 3 4 2026, Date 6 4 2026), (LIST Date 7 4 2026)) EQUALS Date 8 4 2026
-- Holiday means (a) a public holiday in the place AND (b) a day the office is closed for the whole day: either is a holiday.
#ASSERT `is a holiday for the time for doing a thing` (Date 7 4 2026) (`Days of closure` OF EMPTY, (LIST Date 7 4 2026))
#ASSERT `is a holiday for the time for doing a thing` (Date 7 4 2026) (`Days of closure` OF (LIST Date 7 4 2026), EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a holiday for the time for doing a thing` (Date 8 4 2026) (`Days of closure` OF (LIST Date 7 4 2026), (LIST Date 7 4 2026)))
-- The business-day definition (2B) knows only public holidays, not office closures.
#ASSERT `is a business day` (Date 7 4 2026) EMPTY
-- Within the time allowed: the period begins 2026-01-02 and its last day 2026-01-31 is a Saturday.
#ASSERT `the thing is done within the time allowed` (Date 31 1 2026) (Date 2 1 2026) (Date 31 1 2026) `no closures`
#ASSERT `the thing is done within the time allowed` (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 2 1 2026) (Date 31 1 2026) `no closures`
#ASSERT `the thing is done within the time allowed` (Date 2 2 2026) (Date 2 1 2026) (Date 31 1 2026) `no closures`
#ASSERT NOT (`the thing is done within the time allowed` (Date 3 2 2026) (Date 2 1 2026) (Date 31 1 2026) `no closures`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the thing is done within the time allowed` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 2 1 2026) (Date 31 1 2026) `no closures`)
-- Days of rest INSIDE a period still count towards its length (nothing in the text excludes them): 30 days from 2026-01-01 still end on 2026-01-31 though 3 and 4, 10 and 11, ... are weekends.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 30 Days `starting on` (Date 2 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)

§ `Part 3: when an Act comes into operation (ss 3 and 3A)`

-- W7 an Act assented to on 2026-03-10 that says nothing: the 28th day after is 2026-04-07 (3A(2)), at the start of the day (s 3).
#ASSERT `the day the enactment commences` `Act` `silent about commencement` (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 7 4 2026)
#ASSERT `the moment the enactment comes into operation` `Act` `silent about commencement` (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (`Moment in a day` OF (Date 7 4 2026), 0, 0, 0)
-- Month-end arithmetic on the 28 days.
#ASSERT `the day the enactment commences` `Act` `silent about commencement` (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2026)
#ASSERT `the day the enactment commences` `Act` `silent about commencement` (Date 1 2 2024) EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2024)
#ASSERT `the day the enactment commences` `Act` `silent about commencement` (Date 10 12 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 7 1 2026)
-- 3A(3): an Act to alter the Constitution commences on the day of Royal Assent.
#ASSERT `the day the enactment commences` `Act to alter the Constitution` `silent about commencement` (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2026)
-- 3A(1): an Act that provides for its own commencement is not given the 28 days.
#ASSERT `the day the enactment commences` `Act` (`commencement on a particular day` (Date 1 6 2026)) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 6 2026)
-- W8 a day to be fixed later: until it is fixed, no day; once fixed as 2026-06-01, the start of that day (s 3).
#ASSERT `the day the enactment commences` `Act` `commencement on a day still to be fixed` (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the moment the enactment comes into operation` `Act` `commencement on a day still to be fixed` (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the moment the enactment comes into operation` `Act` (`commencement on a day fixed later` (Date 1 6 2026)) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (`Moment in a day` OF (Date 1 6 2026), 0, 0, 0)
-- W9 subordinate legislation made on 2026-03-10 that says nothing: the text gives no default.
#ASSERT `the day the enactment commences` `legislative instrument` `silent about commencement` (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the day the enactment commences` `notifiable instrument` `silent about commencement` (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the day the enactment commences` `other instrument made under a power` `silent about commencement` (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the moment the enactment comes into operation` `legislative instrument` `silent about commencement` (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- An instrument that names a day does come into operation at the start of it.
#ASSERT `the moment the enactment comes into operation` `legislative instrument` (`commencement on a particular day` (Date 1 5 2026)) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (`Moment in a day` OF (Date 1 5 2026), 0, 0, 0)

§ `Part 6: service by post (s 29)`

-- Properly addressed, prepaid, posted as a letter: taken to be effected on the day the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post.
#ASSERT `the day service by post is taken to be effected` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 14 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Date 14 3 2026)
-- Unless the contrary is proved.
#ASSERT `the day service by post is taken to be effected` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 14 3 2026) (JUST (Date 20 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 20 3 2026)
-- Each of the three conditions is needed.
#ASSERT `the day service by post is taken to be effected` FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 14 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the day service by post is taken to be effected` TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 14 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the day service by post is taken to be effected` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 14 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 37A: attaining an age`

-- Born 17 May 2000: attains 18 at the start of 17 May 2018.
#ASSERT `the moment a person attains the age` (Date 17 5 2000) 18 EQUALS JUST (`Moment in a day` OF (Date 17 5 2018), 0, 0, 0)
-- Born 29 February 2000: the 4th and 24th anniversaries fall on leap days; the 1st does not exist.
#ASSERT `the moment a person attains the age` (Date 29 2 2000) 4 EQUALS JUST (`Moment in a day` OF (Date 29 2 2004), 0, 0, 0)
#ASSERT `the moment a person attains the age` (Date 29 2 2000) 24 EQUALS JUST (`Moment in a day` OF (Date 29 2 2024), 0, 0, 0)
#ASSERT `the moment a person attains the age` (Date 29 2 2000) 1 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the moment a person attains the age` (Date 29 2 2000) 100 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the moment a person attains the age` (Date 17 5 2000) 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the moment a person attains the age` (Date 17 5 2000) 2.5 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 2M: sitting day`

`the Senate sits Thursday into Friday` MEANS `A sitting of a House` OF (Date 5 3 2026), (Date 6 3 2026)
`the House sits Wednesday into Thursday` MEANS `A sitting of a House` OF (Date 4 3 2026), (Date 5 3 2026)
`the House sits again on Thursday` MEANS `A sitting of a House` OF (Date 5 3 2026), (Date 5 3 2026)

-- Example 1: the Senate begins sitting on Thursday 2026-03-05 and is adjourned on Friday 2026-03-06: Thursday is a sitting day, Friday is not.
#ASSERT `is a sitting day` (Date 5 3 2026) (LIST `the Senate sits Thursday into Friday`)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a sitting day` (Date 6 3 2026) (LIST `the Senate sits Thursday into Friday`))
-- Example 2: Wednesday 2026-03-04 into Thursday, then a second sitting on Thursday: both are sitting days.
#ASSERT `is a sitting day` (Date 4 3 2026) (LIST `the House sits Wednesday into Thursday`, `the House sits again on Thursday`)
#ASSERT `is a sitting day` (Date 5 3 2026) (LIST `the House sits Wednesday into Thursday`, `the House sits again on Thursday`)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a sitting day` (Date 6 3 2026) (LIST `the House sits Wednesday into Thursday`, `the House sits again on Thursday`))
-- Without the second sitting Thursday is only part of Wednesday's sitting day.
#ASSERT NOT (`is a sitting day` (Date 5 3 2026) (LIST `the House sits Wednesday into Thursday`))

`a sitting on 3 March` MEANS `A sitting of a House` OF (Date 3 3 2026), (Date 3 3 2026)
`a sitting on 4 March` MEANS `A sitting of a House` OF (Date 4 3 2026), (Date 4 3 2026)
`a sitting on 10 March` MEANS `A sitting of a House` OF (Date 10 3 2026), (Date 10 3 2026)
`a second sitting on 10 March` MEANS `A sitting of a House` OF (Date 10 3 2026), (Date 10 3 2026)
`a sitting on 11 March` MEANS `A sitting of a House` OF (Date 11 3 2026), (Date 11 3 2026)
`a sitting on 12 March` MEANS `A sitting of a House` OF (Date 12 3 2026), (Date 12 3 2026)
`a sitting on 17 March` MEANS `A sitting of a House` OF (Date 17 3 2026), (Date 17 3 2026)

`some sittings` MEANS LIST `a sitting on 3 March`, `a sitting on 4 March`, `a sitting on 10 March`, `a second sitting on 10 March`, `a sitting on 11 March`, `a sitting on 12 March`, `a sitting on 17 March`

-- The n-th sitting day after a day (strictly after: s 36(1) item 6). After 4 March the sitting days are 10, 11, 12 and 17 March.
#ASSERT `the sitting day that is the n-th after` 1 (Date 4 3 2026) `some sittings` EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2026)
#ASSERT `the sitting day that is the n-th after` 3 (Date 4 3 2026) `some sittings` EQUALS JUST (Date 12 3 2026)
#ASSERT `the sitting day that is the n-th after` 4 (Date 4 3 2026) `some sittings` EQUALS JUST (Date 17 3 2026)
#ASSERT `the sitting day that is the n-th after` 5 (Date 4 3 2026) `some sittings` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the sitting day that is the n-th after` 0 (Date 4 3 2026) `some sittings` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Two sittings that begin on 10 March are one sitting day: the 2nd sitting day after 9 March is 11 March.
#ASSERT `the sitting day that is the n-th after` 2 (Date 9 3 2026) `some sittings` EQUALS JUST (Date 11 3 2026)
-- Strictly after: the 1st sitting day after 10 March is 11 March.
#ASSERT `the sitting day that is the n-th after` 1 (Date 10 3 2026) `some sittings` EQUALS JUST (Date 11 3 2026)
